---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const consultationUrl = 'https://calendly.com/agnesriley';

const assessmentChecks = [
	'What the system actually does: schema, scripts, integrations, and the workflows your team depends on every day.',
	'What is worth keeping: the FileMaker decisions, shortcuts, and business rules that still fit the way your team works.',
	'What is causing pressure: missing updates, slow screens, fragile scripts, mobile or web expectations, AI requests, and Claris roadmap concerns.',
	'Honest cost ranges: for modernizing in place, for a partial migration, and for a full rebuild.',
];

const deliverables = [
	'A written report you can share with your team, your board, or another vendor.',
	'A recommendation I will defend: keep improving FileMaker, modernize the rough spots, or plan a careful migration.',
	'A working session to walk through it and answer questions.',
];

const proofPoints = [
	'33 years working with FileMaker systems.',
	'Former FileMaker platform product manager at Claris/Apple.',
	'I also build modern web applications with Next.js, React, and cloud infrastructure.',
	'Creator of FMDojo, a FileMaker-focused tool for understanding schema, logs, monitoring, and system risk.',
	'Sometimes my report says "stay on FileMaker." That is the point.',
];

const faqs = [
	{
		question: 'Should I migrate off FileMaker?',
		answer: 'Not automatically. Many FileMaker systems still fit the business well. The right answer depends on what you like about the system, where Claris or the current build is not keeping up, and what changing it would cost.',
	},
	{
		question: 'How much does it cost to migrate from FileMaker?',
		answer: 'A migration cost depends on schema, scripts, integrations, business rules, and workflow complexity. The assessment gives you real ranges for modernizing in place, partial migration, and full rebuild so the decision is based on evidence.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What is a FileMaker alternative?',
		answer: 'A FileMaker alternative might be a custom web application, a SaaS platform, or a hybrid approach that keeps FileMaker where it still fits. The best alternative is the one that matches the workflow without recreating old problems.',
	},
];
---

<PageLayout
	title="Modernize or migrate? Get a straight answer about your FileMaker system | ZeroBlue"
	description="Your FileMaker system still runs the business, but you're wondering how long that lasts. I give current FileMaker teams an honest assessment: keep improving it, modernize the rough spots, or plan a migration."
	heroTitle="Modernize or migrate? Get a straight answer."
	heroSubtitle="Your FileMaker system may still be the best tool your business has. It may also be showing its age: slow updates, missing web or mobile workflows, AI pressure, or frustration that Claris is not moving in the direction you need. I will give you an honest read, including 'keep FileMaker' if that is the right answer."
	heroEyebrow="FileMaker Modernization Assessment"
	faqs={faqs}
>
	<Fragment slot="heroVisual">
		<div class="surface-card overflow-hidden">
			<img
				src="/images/site/filemaker-consulting-workspace.webp"
				alt="FileMaker consulting workspace with database planning notes"
				width="1680"
				height="951"
				class="aspect-[16/11] w-full object-cover"
				loading="eager"
			/>
			<div class="grid gap-3 p-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
				<div class="rounded-xl bg-sky-100 p-4 dark:bg-sky-500/15">
					<p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-200">Modernize</p>
				</div>
				<div class="rounded-xl bg-teal-100 p-4 dark:bg-teal-500/15">
					<p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-200">Migrate</p>
				</div>
				<div class="rounded-xl bg-amber-100 p-4 dark:bg-amber-500/15">
					<p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-200">Keep what works</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Fragment>

	<section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
		<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-stretch">
			<div class="surface-card p-8 lg:p-10">
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">The situation</p>
				<h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
					You are not the only one asking this question.
				</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
					<p>
						A lot of businesses are sitting on FileMaker systems they still like. The system knows the work,
						the team knows the screens, and replacing it casually would be expensive and disruptive. At the same time,
						the requests keep piling up: better web access, cleaner mobile workflows, AI, integrations, reporting,
						or changes Claris has not delivered fast enough for your business.
					</p>
					<p>
						The problem is that everyone you ask has a bias. FileMaker consultants may want to keep you on FileMaker.
						Web agencies may want to rebuild everything. Nobody starts with the question that matters: what does your
						system do well, where is it holding you back, and what would it cost to change that?
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-8">
					<a href={consultationUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-primary">
						Tell me about your system
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="surface-card overflow-hidden">
				<div class="color-strip"></div>
				<div class="p-8 lg:p-10">
					<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">Scoped assessment</p>
					<h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
						The Modernize-or-Migrate Assessment
					</h2>
					<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
						A focused review of your FileMaker system, scoped around the size and complexity of the file. You get a
						written report with a clear recommendation for a current FileMaker environment: keep investing, modernize
						specific weak spots, or plan a migration with your eyes open.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
						<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-300">How scoping works</p>
						<p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white">Start with the conversation</p>
						<p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
							After the first conversation, I will define the assessment scope before work begins.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
		<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
			<div class="surface-card p-8 lg:p-10">
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">What I look at</p>
				<ol class="mt-6 space-y-4">
					{assessmentChecks.map((item, index) => (
						<li class="relative rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 pl-16 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900/70 dark:text-slate-300">
							<span class="absolute left-5 top-5 inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white text-sm font-bold text-sky-700 shadow-sm shadow-slate-900/10 ring-1 ring-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-sky-200 dark:ring-slate-700">
								{index + 1}
							</span>
							{item}
						</li>
					))}
				</ol>
			</div>

			<div class="surface-card p-8 lg:p-10">
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">What you get</p>
				<ul class="mt-6 space-y-4">
					{deliverables.map((item) => (
						<li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900/70 dark:text-slate-300">
							<span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
							<span>{item}</span>
						</li>
					))}
				</ul>
				<div class="mt-8">
					<a href={consultationUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-primary">
						Tell me about your system
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
		<div class="surface-card overflow-hidden">
			<div class="color-strip"></div>
			<div class="grid gap-8 p-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:p-10">
				<div>
					<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">Why me</p>
					<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
						I have seen this decision from every side.
					</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
					{proofPoints.map((point) => (
						<div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 font-semibold leading-7 text-slate-800 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900/70 dark:text-slate-200">
							{point}
						</div>
					))}
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
		<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:items-center">
			<div>
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">FileMaker visibility</p>
				<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
					FMDojo helps make the current system less mysterious.
				</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="surface-card p-8 lg:p-10">
				<p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
					If the right answer is to keep investing in FileMaker, the next problem is usually visibility:
					what changed, what broke, what is risky, and what the server is trying to tell you. I built{' '}
					<a href="https://fmdojo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="accent-link">FMDojo</a>
					{' '}for that work: FileMaker-aware monitoring, log review, and system insight that can support the assessment
					and the modernization work after it.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
		<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-center">
			<div>
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">What happens after</p>
				<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
					The assessment is the whole product. What you do with it is up to you.
				</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="surface-card p-8 lg:p-10">
				<p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
					Some clients take the report and hire their existing team. Some ask me to do the modernization work.
					Some plan a migration over a year or two. The report is designed to be useful no matter who does the
					next step. It is not a sales funnel with only one exit.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<dl class="mt-8 space-y-4">
				{faqs.map((faq) => (
					<div class="surface-card p-6">
						<dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white">{faq.question}</dt>
						<dd class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">{faq.answer}</dd>
					</div>
				))}
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-800 p-8 text-white shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/20 dark:bg-sky-900 lg:p-12">
		<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-center">
			<div>
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-300">Start with a 20-minute conversation</p>
				<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold md:text-4xl">Tell me what has you nervous about the system.</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
					Tell me what the system does, what is making you nervous, and what you have been told so far.
					I will tell you honestly whether the assessment would be worth it for your situation.
				</p>
			</div>
			<a href={consultationUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-primary">
				Tell me about your system
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
